{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304785-fusing-exalted-1e-and-exalted-3e","id":1304785,"title":"Fusing Exalted 1e and Exalted 3e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-14T05:09:02-07:00","id":1304785,"title":"Fusing Exalted 1e and Exalted 3e","content":"I have a confession to make, I love Exalted 1e, warts and all. When I first started playing back in 2004, I thought that the concept was amazing and, while the rules were rather clunky, I had been playing White Wolf products since WtA 1e, so it was not a major issue. I created dozens of home rules to correct issues, made up dozens of campaigns, and ran more than a few of the most enjoyable campaigns in my gaming career. After all, what other world could you have your PCs hire porters who were 12' tall ganja smoking Crocodile People or ally with race of 5' Terrestrial Half-Caste Rabbit Folk?<br /> <br /> Exalted 2e was a disappointment to me. While it had some good parts, such as mortal sorcery and mortal thaumaturgy, it did not feel like Exalted, if you know what I mean. Of course, Infernals really was objectionable, more for the fact that they published an entire hardback book on a group of 50 Exalted rather than the content, though the fluff was tasteless.<br /> <br /> Exalted 3e has a lot going for it though, and I would say that it is equal to 1e in potential. First, Creation is larger than in 1e, and there are more types of Exalted. Second, the sorcery rules are much better than they were in 1e, and you can actually play an effective mortal sorcerer. Third, the combat system, which could be argued to be more realistic than previous Exalted combat systems, as withering-combat could represent tactical position while decisive-combat could represent actual combat. I am not a fan of the Craft system though, but I do not have to use it, so I will not say anything more on that subject.<br /> <br /> Right now, I want to take the best of Exalted 3e and fuse it with Exalted 1e. The changes to Creation, sorcery, and combat will be grafted onto Exalted 1e, along with my own changes to the rules and setting. What else you suggest that I include from 3e in a fusion of 1e and 3e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","user":"The Fool of Creation","date":". 04-14-2019, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T07:45:43-07:00","id":1304808,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of selling points to the withering and decisive setup, but realism isn't one I'd mention. It's meant for a highly stylized experience from out of the movies, or watching someone get S or higher rank in DMC games - a contributor to a visual spectacle. Realism probably wasn't a going concern for its production.<br /> <br /> One of the first things I'd do if I were playing 1e, though, is adopting the mass combat system that encompasses/replaces extras. Why bother having two different systems for few vs many action scenes when you can combine the two and save yourself the trouble of having to write in &quot;is a heroic character capable of stunts&quot; into NPC descriptions ever again, or even the entire concept of extra vs. heroic as a kind of metaphysical concept?<br /> <br /> Also, getting rid of the term Half-Caste. Why that ever got selected to go into a book as an official term, the mind boggles.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T08:43:34-07:00","id":1304813,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Exalted-Blooded would be more acceptable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T09:07:04-07:00","id":1304818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304785-fusing-exalted-1e-and-exalted-3e?p=1304813#post1304813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Exalted-Blooded would be more acceptable?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;[X]-Touched/Blessed/Born&quot; seems to be getting some mileage currently (for example, Starborn, Moon-Blessed, Sun-Touched, et cetera.). Collectively, they might be called the Children of the Mighty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T10:28:42-07:00","id":1304834,"title":"","content":"Well, so could any God-Booded though (I think that was literally one of the names in 2e for God-Blooded). I think that Half-Exalted might be a good enough name for now, at least until another name comes out in 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T10:31:50-07:00","id":1304836,"title":"","content":"Speaking of which, is 3e going the 1e route with having Terrestrial Half-Exalted or is it going the 2e route with not having them around? I have not gotten around to ordering Dragon-Blooded 3e yet, though I probably will after classes end in May.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T10:50:22-07:00","id":1304840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304785-fusing-exalted-1e-and-exalted-3e?p=1304834#post1304834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Half-Exalted might be a good enough name for now, at least until another name comes out in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't particularly see it as fitting, considering that per dev statements, the children of Exalts aren't granted copies of their parents' Charmsets, nor are they even assumed to have Charms by default. They're made special by dint of having been steeped in Exalted Essence since before they were born, but calling them &quot;Half-Exalted&quot; is misrepresenting them.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd no, no Dragon-Touched in Ex3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-14-2019, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T10:56:18-07:00","id":1304843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304785-fusing-exalted-1e-and-exalted-3e?p=1304836#post1304836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, is 3e going the 1e route with having Terrestrial Half-Exalted or is it going the 2e route with not having them around? I have not gotten around to ordering Dragon-Blooded 3e yet, though I probably will after classes end in May.</div> </div> </div> </div>You either become a Dragon-Blood or you don\u2019t. If you don\u2019t, you\u2019re better breeding stock than a random mortal but still not as good as a Dragon-Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}